{"name":"Torii Red","hex":"#db3e00","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"torii","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A traditional Japanese gate at Shinto shrines, symbolically marking the transition from the profane to the sacred."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of torus"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/torii"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Torii","blocks":[{"text":"A torii  is a traditional Japanese gate most commonly found at the entrance of, or within, a Shinto shrine, where it symbolically marks the transition from the mundane to the sacred, and a spot where kami are welcomed and thought to travel through."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/ItsukushimaTorii7379.jpg/330px-ItsukushimaTorii7379.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Torii"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Hogonji13s3200.jpg/500px-Hogonji13s3200.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Hogonji13s3200.jpg/1280px-Hogonji13s3200.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Hogonji13s3200.jpg/500px-Hogonji13s3200.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Buddhist goddess Benzaiten, a torii visible on her head","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHogonji13s3200.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Monument_at_Sanchi_Stupa_India_24.jpg/250px-Monument_at_Sanchi_Stupa_India_24.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Monument_at_Sanchi_Stupa_India_24.jpg/330px-Monument_at_Sanchi_Stupa_India_24.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Monument_at_Sanchi_Stupa_India_24.jpg/250px-Monument_at_Sanchi_Stupa_India_24.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonument_at_Sanchi_Stupa_India_24.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Temple0136.JPG/250px-Temple0136.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Temple0136.JPG/330px-Temple0136.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x